INFO:agent.loop:\u26a1 Executing tool: 'knowledge_agent' with arguments: {"source_title": "Internet Research Agency Indictment", "source_url": "https://www.justice.gov/d9/fieldable-panel-panes/basic-panes/attachments/2018/02/16/internet_research_agency_indictment.pdf", "text": "DOJ indictment alleges IRA was a Russian organization engaged in election/political interference. From 2014 it targeted the 2016 U.S. presidential election. It alleges funding from Yevgeniy Prigozhin and companies he controlled, Concord Management and Consulting and Concord Catering; Concord was primary funding source and monthly Project Lakhta budget exceeded 73 million rubles (over $1.25m) by September 2016. Employees posed as U.S. persons, created false U.S. personas, operated divisive political/social pages and groups, used stolen identities, bought social-media political ads, staged U.S. rallies, solicited/compensated U.S. persons, and sought coordination with unwitting campaign/activists. Strategic goal alleged: sow discord; by early/mid-2016 support Trump and disparage Clinton. Translator project operated on YouTube, Facebook, Instagram, Twitter; over 80 employees by July 2016; strategy included spreading distrust toward candidates and political system. IRA had hundreds of employees, millions-dollar annual budget, and described its activity as information warfare against the United States. Indictment allegations are not convictions."}
